# SDD execution scratch (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Planning history (specs and plans) — kept locally, not in the repo.
# The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `docs` matches ANY directory of that name at any
# depth, including `src/components/docs/`. Tailwind v4's `@source` honours .gitignore, so that
# pattern silently drops the /docs gallery's classes from the stylesheet (measured: 24,595 ->
# 23,275 bytes) and the page renders unstyled with every gate still green.
/docs/

# Agent tool state, same category as .superpowers/ above. Only the local-only file, so a
# project-level .claude/ config can still be committed if the team ever wants one.
#
# This is ignored by many developers' global git excludes already, but Biome's `useIgnoreFile`
# reads THIS file and not the global one, and the root biome.json lints `**`. Without the entry
# here, `pnpm verify` fails on a file the harness rewrites whenever a permission is granted.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The web build embedded into the Go binary (see apps/api/internal/static/static.go). Everything
# in it is a build artifact except dist/.placeholder, which is committed so `//go:embed all:dist`
# has something to match on a fresh clone.
#
# Three lines, not the two this looks like it should need. The bare `dist` rule at the top of this
# file already excludes this directory outright (verified with `git check-ignore -v`), and a
# directory excluded that way cannot be reopened by a file-level negation below it -- git will not
# even descend into it to check. The first line here re-admits the directory itself so the next
# two can then exclude its contents and re-admit exactly the placeholder, the same two-line shape
# used everywhere else in this file for a directory that is mostly, but not entirely, ignored.
!apps/api/internal/static/dist/
apps/api/internal/static/dist/*
!apps/api/internal/static/dist/.placeholder
